WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
House of the Dragon teaser trailer is out,&nbsp;
leaving many of you excited for what’s to come,
&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.480
but also leaving some of you confused&nbsp;
about certain things, but don’t worry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.000
this is why we decided to make an explanation&nbsp;
video, explaining everything and more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.680
bringing some things to your attention which&nbsp;
you may have missed. First things first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.040
let’s explain what House of the Dragon is about.
It’s about a Targaryen civil war that saw the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.320
of many Targaryens and most of their dragons.
It nearly destroyed their entire house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.920
The series is based on George R.R. Martin’s book&nbsp;
Fire And Blood which covers the entire Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.520
history in Westeros. The prequel series House&nbsp;
of the Dragon finds the Targaryen dynasty at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.440
absolute apex of its power, with around 20 dragons&nbsp;
flying over King’s Landing and Dragonstone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.720
Targaryen’s slow fall begins almost 192 years&nbsp;
before the events of Game of Thrones, when King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.160
Viserys Targaryen breaks with a century of&nbsp;
tradition by naming his daughter Rhaenyra heir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:05.040
to the Iron Throne. But when Viserys later fathers&nbsp;
a son, the court is shocked that Rhaenyra retains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.600
her status as his heir, and seeds of division sow&nbsp;
friction across the realm. So, basically, the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.960
starts with King Viserys I Targaryen sitting on&nbsp;
the Iron Throne with Rhaenyra, his oldest child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.640
being his heir instead of his son Aegon,&nbsp;
much to the displeasure of Aegon’s mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.000
Queen Alicent Hightower. The real trouble starts&nbsp;
when King Viserys dies in the end of season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.960
leading to a Targaryen civil war over&nbsp;
who should be the next king or queen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.520
with half of Westeros siding with Aegon&nbsp;
and the other half with Rhaenyra.
&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.120
But back to the season 1 events&nbsp;
covered by this teaser. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.960
you can see Daemon Targaryen with a torch walking&nbsp;
through the dragonglass cave of Dragonstone. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.000
Ramin Djawadi’s music in the background, we then&nbsp;
hear Daemon Targaryen pronouncing ominous words:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:59.280
“Gods. Kings.Fire. And Blood. Dreams didn’t make&nbsp;
us kings, dragons did.”, referring to Aegon the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.120
Conqueror’s dream to conquer the Seven Kingdoms&nbsp;
as well as about Daenys’ dream to escape Valyria.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.400
As he speaks, you see a succession of quick&nbsp;
shots: Daemon and older version of Rhaenyra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.480
Targaryen on Driftmark shore. These two, uncle&nbsp;
and niece who eventually become husband and wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.360
are the main characters in the series. 
Next is Aegon the Conqueror’s dragon - Balerion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.280
the Black Dread’s skull. The dragon recently died&nbsp;
of old age with King Viserys himself being his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:33.600
last rider. This is his resting place. Then you&nbsp;
see a shot of the Hand of the King. It’s Ser Otto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:39.280
Hightower. Besides being hand to King Viserys,&nbsp;
he is also the father of the king’s wife, Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:45.040
Alicent Hightower who we later see with a dagger.&nbsp;
It’s the very same dagger that Arya used to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:51.440
the Night King 200 years after. As you can see,&nbsp;
Alicent is in distress, caused by this very same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:57.680
dagger that was used by Rhaenyra’s child against&nbsp;
Alicent’s child. When Prince Aemond Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:04.000
attempted to ride Vhagar, one of House Targaryen's&nbsp;
dragons, he was confronted by Rhaenyra’s children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.440
Aemond broke the nose of five-year-old Luke, who&nbsp;
eventually took out Aemond's eye with his dagger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.840
and here’s his mother Alicent&nbsp;
demanding justice from King Viserys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.960
demanding an eye for an eye. This puts King&nbsp;
Viserys in a hard spot as Aemond is his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.800
but Lucerys is his grandson. Behind Alicent&nbsp;
you can see two members of the Kingsguard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.480
one being Ser Harrold Westerling and the other&nbsp;
being Ser Criston Cole, he himself becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.320
major Alicent’s supporter after falling off with&nbsp;
Princess Rhaenyra. Speaking of the King Viserys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.640
here you have a shot of him sitting on the&nbsp;
Iron Throne with a Targaryen ring on his finger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:49.520
as he holds Blackfyre, one of two of House&nbsp;
Targaryen’s ancestral Valyrian steel swords.
&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.400
If you look closely you’ll notice that he is&nbsp;
also equipped with a Valyrian steel dagger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.680
the same dagger we just saw in Alicent’s&nbsp;
hand. Before it ended up in Alicent’s hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:05.200
King Viserys gave it to his grandson Lucerys&nbsp;
as a gift who then attacked his son with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.440
Back to the sword. Blackfyre is the&nbsp;
sword wielded by Aegon the Conqueror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.800
which was passed down from king to king&nbsp;
and finally you see it in its full glory. 
&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.160
It ‘s got the crossguard fashioned as a pair of&nbsp;
dragon heads with dragon wings. At its pummel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:26.400
you can see Seven Pointed star, a decoration that&nbsp;
did not exist when Aegon the Conqueror wielded it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.520
but was added by King Jaehaerys, the symbol&nbsp;
of the King being the defender of the faith.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.200
There you can also see young Rhaenyra who&nbsp;
is appointed by her father to be his heir.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.240
Followed by a shot of older Rhaenyra&nbsp;
who is accompanied by Daemon Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.400
this time she is not at King’s Landing&nbsp;
where she used to be when she was younger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.320
She is now at Driftmark, the seat of House&nbsp;
Velaryon, attending the funeral of Daemon’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.080
second wife. Both of them are visibly sad as it&nbsp;
was Daemon’s wife and Rhaenyra’s good friend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.600
Then you see a fight scene that takes place&nbsp;
earlier in the story, between Daemon and Criston&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.920
Cole, giving you the first look at Targaryen&nbsp;
armor, helmet, shield as well as Dark Sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.800
a famous sword of House Targaryen once wielded&nbsp;
by Aegon the Conqueror’s sister Visenya.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:20.960
Dark Sister has the crossguard fashioned as a&nbsp;
pair of dragon wings with a head being at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:27.600
base of the blade. Daemon wears the dragon helm,&nbsp;
the same one Rhaegar wore at the Trident when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:33.760
fought Robert Baratheon. The armor is also the&nbsp;
same except Rhaegar had rubies attached to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:39.280
His opponent Criston Cole is an exceptionally&nbsp;
skilled warrior, himself along with Daemon being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:45.040
the best warriors of this time, and Criston&nbsp;
is particularly skilled with his morningstar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:49.920
which you can see here as well. It’s the&nbsp;
tourney for King Viserys I's accession&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:56.160
where in the final fight Ser Criston Cole fights&nbsp;
his final opponent Prince Daemon Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:02.080
and actually wins by knocking aside Daemon’s Dark&nbsp;
Sister with his morningstar. He then gives the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:07.600
victor's laurel to young Princess Rhaenyra&nbsp;
Targaryen. Criston subsequently becomes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:14.080
favorite at court and joins the Kingsguard. Next&nbsp;
up is Corlys Velaryon, known as the Sea Snake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:20.000
a fabled Lord of the Tides, Master of Driftmark,&nbsp;
and the head of House Velaryon who comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:27.040
the old Valyria much like Targaryens. He’s one of&nbsp;
Rhaenyra’s supporters and a good friend of Daemon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:34.080
having one child married to Rhaenyra and the other&nbsp;
to Daemon. He himself is the husband of Princess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.680
Rhaenys Targaryen and here you see a shot of the&nbsp;
Velaryon family entering the Iron Throne room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:46.560
looking rich and powerful as they truly are.&nbsp;
On the left is Sea Snake’s nephew Ser Vaemond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:52.560
the older lady is his wife Rhaenys Targaryen known&nbsp;
as the Queen that never was and the other two are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.800
his children, Laenor and Laena. You can also see&nbsp;
more of Velaryons in the background. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.880
arriving here because the Sea Snake’s son, Laenor,&nbsp;
is being married to the King’s daughter, Rhaenyra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:10.800
and this is their wedding feast. You can see both&nbsp;
Targaryen and Velaryon flags hanging behind them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.240
with all the important lords and ladies&nbsp;
attending the feast. To avoid confusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:22.160
Rhaenys has silver hair instead of black which she&nbsp;
has in the books, indicating she has a Valyrian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:28.560
look and is a Targaryen, while Mysaria has black&nbsp;
hair instead of white as she does in the books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.080
making it clear she’s not of Valyrian descent.
She’s a dancer from Lys who became the paramour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:40.000
of Prince Daemon Targaryen and the unofficial&nbsp;
mistress of whisperers to Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.200
during the Dance of the Dragons. Then we&nbsp;
have another tourney where you can see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:50.160
all sorts of banners including House Stark and&nbsp;
House Lannister. This is a great tourney on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.600
fifth anniversary of King Viserys I and Queen&nbsp;
Alicent's marriage at King's Landing. The reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:01.200
you see Tarly banners on the wall is because Ser&nbsp;
Criston Cole is fighting a Tarly in this round.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.000
It’s during the opening feast of this very same&nbsp;
tourney that Queen Alicent wore a green gown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.520
while Princess Rhaenyra dressed in the red&nbsp;
and black of House Targaryen. Note was taken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.560
and thereafter it became the custom to refer to&nbsp;
"greens" and "blacks" when talking of the queen's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:22.000
party and the party of the princess, respectively.&nbsp;
Prince Daemon Targaryen returns to King's Landing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:27.520
as King during this tourney from his wars at&nbsp;
the Stepstones to swear fealty to his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:34.080
King Viserys I Targaryen. This little shot&nbsp;
is of Ser Criston Cole unhorsing Tarly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.880
Then you have another fighting scene, this&nbsp;
time between the Sea Snake’s son, Laenor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:44.960
and Laenor’s friend and lover Ser Qarl Correy,&nbsp;
which will not go well to say the least. Young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:50.720
Rhaenyra is then visiting her father King Viserys&nbsp;
where you see a new version of the Iron Throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:56.080
It’s not exactly all new as the chair itself&nbsp;
remains the same, but it’s surrounded by new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.280
swords, making it look a little bit closer&nbsp;
to what the Iron Throne looks in the books.
&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.000
In order to stay true to the look the Iron&nbsp;
Throne had in Game of Thrones, but also get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:11.120
a little closer to the look the Iron Throne has&nbsp;
in the books, it’s been decided to add the swords&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.880
around the throne, thus making it a bit closer&nbsp;
to the books. The swords that were once wielded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:22.000
against Aegon the Conqueror are now defending the&nbsp;
Targaryen kings on the throne. This is where we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.880
come to an end, but before we end it, I would just&nbsp;
like to reveal to you that the filming of season 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:32.880
is still ongoing and will be finished next month,&nbsp;
when it enters post production and soon after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:39.200
airs on HBO. All of this and more you will see in&nbsp;
2022 on HBO. Thank you so much for watching. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:49.840
you enjoyed this video please give it a big thumbs&nbsp;
up and I hope to see you in the next one, peace!

